00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:03,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:00:04,105 --> 00:00:07,425
Lazy Meow Meow,
is competing at Siam for the first time!

2
00:00:08,505 --> 00:00:11,345
I'm glad we're talking
like we used to again.

3
00:00:11,425 --> 00:00:13,105
Just getting your support

4
00:00:13,185 --> 00:00:15,825
was enough to help me chase my dream.

5
00:00:15,905 --> 00:00:17,025
I came over to say hi, LeeIth.

6
00:00:17,105 --> 00:00:20,425
I think, this one isn't hiding it.

7
00:00:20,945 --> 00:00:22,145
I think

8
00:00:22,225 --> 00:00:23,345
you might have feelings for Jia.

9
00:00:23,425 --> 00:00:25,145
Honestly, I feel that way too.

10
00:00:25,225 --> 00:00:27,225
If you ever feel sad, just be sad.

11
00:00:27,305 --> 00:00:28,785
People can't control their feelings.

12
00:00:28,865 --> 00:00:31,225
Besides Indy, you're my best friend too.

13
00:00:32,705 --> 00:00:34,345
I'm going back to Chiang Mai.

14
00:00:35,145 --> 00:00:36,425
Tell Mom and Dad for me.

15
00:00:50,545 --> 00:00:52,145
Stop acting cool. Hurry up.

16
00:00:53,785 --> 00:00:55,785
-I know.
-Hurry up. Come on.

17
00:01:03,665 --> 00:01:04,704
Okay, let's go.

18
00:01:26,865 --> 00:01:30,345
Mom, I wish you good health
and that you get prettier every day.

19
00:01:30,425 --> 00:01:32,225
How sweet.

20
00:01:32,305 --> 00:01:34,545
And I hope you get
a thousand times richer,

21
00:01:34,625 --> 00:01:36,105
so we can finally travel abroad together.

22
00:01:36,185 --> 00:01:37,305
Huh?

23
00:01:38,025 --> 00:01:39,065
Hey, Sis.

24
00:01:39,145 --> 00:01:41,225
You've lived abroad for ages.
What more do you want?

25
00:01:41,305 --> 00:01:43,545
Well, I went alone. I'm bored of that.

26
00:01:43,625 --> 00:01:45,425
Next time, we all have to go together.

27
00:01:47,185 --> 00:01:49,945
Okay, great. All right, everyone,
let's sing together.

28
00:01:55,905 --> 00:01:56,825
I'll blow out the candles now.

29
00:02:36,505 --> 00:02:38,265
What is this? You're creeping me out.

30
00:02:38,345 --> 00:02:40,225
Let me get a photo with the hot guy.

31
00:02:40,305 --> 00:02:42,825
You just transferred
to Watthana Kunlaya School,

32
00:02:42,905 --> 00:02:44,665
and you already gained
a thousand followers.

33
00:02:44,745 --> 00:02:45,825
I'm so confused.

34
00:02:45,905 --> 00:02:49,185
Well, this super handsome guy

35
00:02:49,265 --> 00:02:50,625
is your little brother.

36
00:02:57,265 --> 00:03:00,105
Hey, have you told Mom and Dad yet?

37
00:03:03,825 --> 00:03:04,705
Not yet.

38
00:03:05,865 --> 00:03:07,185
I'll help you.

39
00:03:07,265 --> 00:03:09,065
-No!
-Mom, Dad,

40
00:03:09,145 --> 00:03:10,625
Lee wants to talk to you.

41
00:03:11,585 --> 00:03:12,745
-Wait a second.
-Go ahead.

42
00:03:15,065 --> 00:03:16,265
What is it, sweetheart?

43
00:03:22,425 --> 00:03:23,505
Mom.

44
00:03:23,585 --> 00:03:24,585
Yes, honey?

45
00:03:25,665 --> 00:03:26,865
Well,

46
00:03:27,945 --> 00:03:29,865
I wanted to ask,

47
00:03:30,705 --> 00:03:33,065
if I really want to be a musician,

48
00:03:34,545 --> 00:03:36,145
would you mind?

49
00:03:40,985 --> 00:03:44,265
I'll be honest, I'm hesitant too.

50
00:03:45,505 --> 00:03:48,745
Because you're the type
to get bored with things quickly.

51
00:03:51,665 --> 00:03:53,945
But when I saw you onstage,

52
00:03:56,185 --> 00:03:59,705
I realized what truly makes you happy.

53
00:04:01,145 --> 00:04:02,385
Onstage?

54
00:04:03,825 --> 00:04:05,025
When did you see that?

55
00:04:05,665 --> 00:04:07,065
Mom shared it all over Facebook.

56
00:04:07,145 --> 00:04:08,345
Didn't you see it?

57
00:04:09,065 --> 00:04:10,265
Facebook?

58
00:04:10,345 --> 00:04:11,545
Who even uses that anymore?

59
00:04:11,625 --> 00:04:13,465
Only old people use Facebook.

60
00:04:13,545 --> 00:04:17,345
Well, it's old people like us
who support our kids.

61
00:04:19,145 --> 00:04:21,665
That Instagram thing is too hard.

62
00:04:21,745 --> 00:04:24,065
We aunties aren't good with it.

63
00:04:24,145 --> 00:04:27,385
We just follow the links your mom shares.

64
00:04:27,985 --> 00:04:28,905
But you're good.

65
00:04:28,985 --> 00:04:30,185
You even came in second.

66
00:04:30,265 --> 00:04:32,105
-Yeah, that's right.
-Amazing.

67
00:04:32,625 --> 00:04:35,425
Great job, Son.
I even liked it on Facebook.

68
00:04:38,665 --> 00:04:41,025
Wait, you all saw it?

69
00:04:41,105 --> 00:04:43,465
Yeah, we all saw it.

70
00:04:43,545 --> 00:04:45,385
And I'm so proud of you.

71
00:04:46,905 --> 00:04:50,625
If you want to study music,
I'll support you.

72
00:04:51,305 --> 00:04:52,305
I only ask one thing.

73
00:04:52,385 --> 00:04:54,305
Don't do anything halfheartedly.

74
00:04:56,145 --> 00:04:57,865
You can do it, Son. I'm rooting for you.

75
00:04:58,385 --> 00:05:01,065
Aw, Mom, Dad.

76
00:05:01,145 --> 00:05:02,505
Don't make me emotional.

77
00:05:03,105 --> 00:05:04,545
You're so sensitive.

78
00:06:21,825 --> 00:06:22,985
Dad, look.

79
00:06:27,865 --> 00:06:28,785
Here.

80
00:06:32,145 --> 00:06:32,985
Huh?

81
00:06:33,065 --> 00:06:34,545
Aren't you taking it to the uncles?

82
00:06:35,265 --> 00:06:36,265
It's for you.

83
00:06:36,345 --> 00:06:39,585
Practice so you'll know your limit,
how much it takes to get you drunk.

84
00:06:41,905 --> 00:06:42,745
Here.

85
00:06:48,825 --> 00:06:50,785
It's so damn bitter.
How do you guys drink this?

86
00:06:52,105 --> 00:06:54,225
When you grow up, it'll taste sweet.

87
00:06:54,305 --> 00:06:55,185
That's right.

88
00:06:55,265 --> 00:06:57,665
Because once life's bitter,
a cold beer is the best thing ever.

89
00:06:58,745 --> 00:07:00,145
That's a bit much.

90
00:07:01,145 --> 00:07:02,905
I'll take this to the uncles.

91
00:07:07,545 --> 00:07:08,545
Hi.

92
00:07:09,185 --> 00:07:11,345
Want some snacks too, you drunks?

93
00:07:11,425 --> 00:07:13,545
You started drinking before sunset.

94
00:07:17,745 --> 00:07:20,945
Seriously, is there anything else
you want to tell us?

95
00:07:22,105 --> 00:07:24,625
We've already talked about school,

96
00:07:25,225 --> 00:07:27,145
and we can talk about love too.

97
00:07:33,585 --> 00:07:35,345
-I…
-Wait.

98
00:07:35,425 --> 00:07:37,265
I'll take them some snacks first.

99
00:07:37,345 --> 00:07:38,985
I'll be back. Wait for me.

100
00:07:44,305 --> 00:07:45,945
We're back.

101
00:07:46,745 --> 00:07:47,945
Okay, we're ready.

102
00:07:55,305 --> 00:07:57,865
That's enough. You'll get drunk
and we won't understand you.

103
00:07:57,945 --> 00:07:59,065
-Dad, you too.
-Huh?

104
00:08:10,145 --> 00:08:13,345
Well, I'm wondering…

105
00:08:15,625 --> 00:08:17,665
When you date a friend

106
00:08:19,465 --> 00:08:20,305
and you break up,

107
00:08:22,625 --> 00:08:24,185
then go back to being friends,

108
00:08:25,825 --> 00:08:27,345
but no matter what,

109
00:08:27,425 --> 00:08:29,785
you can't really be friends
with your ex again.

110
00:08:32,264 --> 00:08:33,825
Dad, Mom, Sis, what would you do?

111
00:08:34,664 --> 00:08:37,144
Don't tell me you dated Indy.

112
00:08:38,144 --> 00:08:40,425
I'm gonna puke. No.

113
00:08:41,705 --> 00:08:44,785
I bet it's Putter.

114
00:08:46,225 --> 00:08:47,505
Right?

115
00:08:50,265 --> 00:08:53,345
I've known for ages.
I was waiting for you to tell us.

116
00:08:54,265 --> 00:08:55,345
At least it's not Indy.

117
00:08:55,985 --> 00:08:57,465
That's not the point, Dad.

118
00:08:59,985 --> 00:09:01,425
But I like Putter.

119
00:09:02,745 --> 00:09:05,985
He seems serious and more responsible.

120
00:09:06,585 --> 00:09:07,665
His grades are good.

121
00:09:07,745 --> 00:09:10,105
He studies hard and still does activities.

122
00:09:11,585 --> 00:09:13,505
Is there anything you don't know, Mom?

123
00:09:15,545 --> 00:09:19,505
So, you guys don't mind

124
00:09:21,145 --> 00:09:22,665
that I like…

125
00:09:28,665 --> 00:09:31,025
These days,
there's nothing strange about it.

126
00:09:31,105 --> 00:09:33,665
Like whoever you want. We don't mind.

127
00:09:35,305 --> 00:09:36,225
Just like your dad.

128
00:09:36,865 --> 00:09:40,305
The moment he saw me,
he knew I was the one.

129
00:09:40,385 --> 00:09:43,585
Then he chased after me,
and here we are 20 years later.

130
00:09:43,665 --> 00:09:45,705
Come on, you're really feeling yourself.

131
00:09:45,785 --> 00:09:48,065
Shouldn't Dad be the one
telling that story, Mom?

132
00:09:50,505 --> 00:09:53,825
Whoever you date,
if they hold you back in life,

133
00:09:54,345 --> 00:09:56,465
that's when we'd see it as a problem.

134
00:09:59,585 --> 00:10:01,185
Talk to Putter again.

135
00:10:01,785 --> 00:10:03,385
Try to understand each other,

136
00:10:03,465 --> 00:10:05,105
and don't force yourself.

137
00:10:05,705 --> 00:10:08,385
If you still like him,
just tell him you like him.

138
00:10:09,225 --> 00:10:10,505
But if you don't, don't force it.

139
00:10:10,585 --> 00:10:12,465
If you don't want to be friends,
that's okay too.

140
00:10:12,545 --> 00:10:14,585
Forcing it will only hurt everyone, right?

141
00:10:14,665 --> 00:10:15,825
No one will be happy.

142
00:11:14,345 --> 00:11:15,425
Te.

143
00:11:15,945 --> 00:11:17,225
Is Putter with you?

144
00:11:17,745 --> 00:11:19,785
No, he's not. Why?

145
00:11:44,905 --> 00:11:46,305
He's flying back to Chiang Mai,

146
00:11:47,105 --> 00:11:48,665
and it looks like he's not coming back.

147
00:11:48,745 --> 00:11:50,465
What? He's not coming back?

148
00:11:51,745 --> 00:11:54,105
Do you know his flight number and time?

149
00:11:59,145 --> 00:12:00,265
TAXI

150
00:13:15,105 --> 00:13:16,185
Hello?

151
00:13:16,825 --> 00:13:17,865
Where are you?

152
00:13:18,385 --> 00:13:19,545
Lee.

153
00:13:24,305 --> 00:13:25,785
What are you doing here?

154
00:13:58,465 --> 00:14:01,305
Putter, I'm sorry.

155
00:14:02,945 --> 00:14:04,185
For what?

156
00:14:04,265 --> 00:14:06,545
Wait. Have you been drinking beer?

157
00:14:07,825 --> 00:14:10,745
You see, I really can't
be friends with you.

158
00:14:12,105 --> 00:14:14,745
I'm the kind of person who,
once I love someone, I love them.

159
00:14:15,705 --> 00:14:19,665
And how I feel right now
is more than friendship.

160
00:14:19,745 --> 00:14:21,345
That's easy for you to say.

161
00:14:21,865 --> 00:14:23,145
I saw you've moved on.

162
00:14:23,665 --> 00:14:24,985
I saw you talking to someone new.

163
00:14:25,065 --> 00:14:27,705
No, I was talking to Chompoo

164
00:14:27,785 --> 00:14:29,865
because she's with a record label,

165
00:14:29,945 --> 00:14:31,545
and I just want an internship.

166
00:14:31,625 --> 00:14:32,745
Seriously.

167
00:14:32,825 --> 00:14:34,145
Believe me.

168
00:14:38,465 --> 00:14:40,505
What about the matching keychains?

169
00:14:41,025 --> 00:14:43,465
You even crumpled up
the picture I drew for you.

170
00:14:48,785 --> 00:14:50,465
That's because
I was trying to get over you.

171
00:14:52,785 --> 00:14:54,225
But I just can't.

172
00:14:54,905 --> 00:14:56,545
Because every time I'm around you

173
00:14:57,545 --> 00:14:59,225
and try to be just friends,

174
00:15:03,825 --> 00:15:05,025
I still can't move on.

175
00:15:11,385 --> 00:15:14,305
I'm begging you.
Don't run away to Chiang Mai.

176
00:15:14,905 --> 00:15:16,145
Give me another chance.

177
00:15:18,105 --> 00:15:19,105
I mean…

178
00:15:22,985 --> 00:15:24,345
You and me,

179
00:15:26,585 --> 00:15:27,865
can we get back together?

180
00:15:42,145 --> 00:15:43,585
I'm not running away from you.

181
00:15:45,585 --> 00:15:47,665
Honestly, I'm the same as you.

182
00:15:49,265 --> 00:15:50,945
I really can't go back
to being your friend.

183
00:15:53,185 --> 00:15:56,585
But, I still have to go home.

184
00:15:56,665 --> 00:15:57,945
Huh?

185
00:15:58,025 --> 00:16:00,465
Why? Won't you give me a chance?

186
00:16:01,185 --> 00:16:02,425
It's not like that.

187
00:16:04,305 --> 00:16:05,585
I mean,

188
00:16:05,665 --> 00:16:08,265
if we feel the same,
you don't have to go back, right?

189
00:16:08,345 --> 00:16:09,945
Listen to me first.

190
00:16:10,025 --> 00:16:12,505
-Don't be so cruel to me.
-Listen to me first.

191
00:16:14,985 --> 00:16:16,265
I just have to go see my grandma.

192
00:16:21,065 --> 00:16:22,705
Are you on break yet?

193
00:16:23,785 --> 00:16:25,185
Grandma's in the hospital.

194
00:16:25,265 --> 00:16:27,625
ARE YOU ON BREAK YET?
GRANDMA'S IN THE HOSPITAL.

195
00:16:31,625 --> 00:16:35,065
I'm going back to Chiang Mai.
Tell Mom and Dad for me.

196
00:16:38,145 --> 00:16:39,585
But I still have to go back.

197
00:16:40,825 --> 00:16:42,505
I've already booked my ticket too.

198
00:16:42,585 --> 00:16:44,345
I thought you were mad at me,

199
00:16:44,425 --> 00:16:46,705
so you were getting back at me
by moving back to Chiang Mai.

200
00:16:49,145 --> 00:16:52,105
But Te said you weren't coming back here.

201
00:16:52,185 --> 00:16:53,145
What's that about?

202
00:16:55,905 --> 00:16:57,985
I might have to transfer schools.

203
00:16:59,065 --> 00:17:00,025
Transfer schools?

204
00:17:01,185 --> 00:17:02,425
I'm still not sure.

205
00:17:03,065 --> 00:17:06,224
But I'll go talk to my family
and rethink my future.

206
00:17:06,305 --> 00:17:09,505
Because, architecture isn't for me anyway.

207
00:17:11,424 --> 00:17:14,184
But if your dream is to play esports,

208
00:17:15,145 --> 00:17:16,585
can't you stay here?

209
00:17:18,665 --> 00:17:21,385
Well, if my family isn't okay with it,

210
00:17:22,464 --> 00:17:24,825
I… might not come back here.

211
00:17:37,185 --> 00:17:39,025
At least I know you feel the same way.

212
00:17:40,945 --> 00:17:42,625
No matter what happens,

213
00:17:45,705 --> 00:17:48,265
I'll always be your number one supporter.

214
00:17:53,025 --> 00:17:55,665
I… don't want you to wait for me.

215
00:17:56,665 --> 00:17:57,585
No.

216
00:17:58,225 --> 00:17:59,905
Call me stubborn if you want,

217
00:18:00,865 --> 00:18:01,865
but I'll wait for you.

218
00:18:03,065 --> 00:18:04,665
I'll wait until you come back.

219
00:18:07,225 --> 00:18:08,265
And we'll…

220
00:18:11,345 --> 00:18:12,625
get back together.

221
00:18:16,465 --> 00:18:18,505
But if your family won't let you,

222
00:18:19,425 --> 00:18:20,905
I'll go straight to your house.

223
00:18:23,505 --> 00:18:24,865
I'll sort it out myself.

224
00:18:26,745 --> 00:18:28,425
You really won't give up, will you?

225
00:18:28,505 --> 00:18:29,985
You're so damn stubborn.

226
00:18:30,065 --> 00:18:31,185
So…

227
00:18:32,785 --> 00:18:33,825
what's your answer?

228
00:18:35,785 --> 00:18:36,905
Figure it out yourself.

229
00:18:36,985 --> 00:18:38,145
It's pretty obvious.

230
00:18:55,545 --> 00:18:56,785
Thanks, Putter.

231
00:18:58,865 --> 00:18:59,865
Yeah.

232
00:19:00,465 --> 00:19:01,705
I'll video call you.

233
00:19:02,305 --> 00:19:04,225
But I'm gonna miss my flight now.

234
00:19:04,825 --> 00:19:05,665
It's okay.

235
00:19:05,745 --> 00:19:07,105
I'll buy you a new ticket.

236
00:19:08,505 --> 00:19:09,585
You talk like you're rich.

237
00:19:10,105 --> 00:19:12,745
If you really have money,
why not buy a ticket and come with me?

238
00:19:14,625 --> 00:19:16,265
-I'm going now.
-Yeah.

239
00:19:36,345 --> 00:19:38,905
I'm off. Good luck. Bye.

240
00:19:44,225 --> 00:19:46,145
Wanna take a trip during break?

241
00:19:46,225 --> 00:19:47,505
How about the beach?

242
00:19:48,345 --> 00:19:49,585
Will your family let you go?

243
00:19:50,705 --> 00:19:51,785
No problem.

244
00:19:51,865 --> 00:19:53,905
I can help Mom at home afterward.

245
00:19:54,865 --> 00:19:57,665
So, you're talking to me,

246
00:19:57,745 --> 00:19:58,865
but you're not talking to Faye?

247
00:19:59,585 --> 00:20:01,065
I don't know what to say to her.

248
00:20:05,305 --> 00:20:06,145
That's weird.

249
00:20:07,225 --> 00:20:08,065
What?

250
00:20:09,665 --> 00:20:10,545
The Lovers card fell out.

251
00:20:12,745 --> 00:20:15,345
Does that mean
you're gonna have a girlfriend?

252
00:20:15,425 --> 00:20:18,145
Well, if it's about love,

253
00:20:18,985 --> 00:20:20,305
it's like I'm about to find something new.

254
00:20:21,105 --> 00:20:23,545
But it's also about making a choice.

255
00:20:23,625 --> 00:20:25,545
If I choose wrong, I'm screwed.

256
00:20:27,985 --> 00:20:30,465
But, it's probably nothing.

257
00:20:46,465 --> 00:20:49,825
I don't think dating someone close to you
is a good idea.

258
00:20:50,625 --> 00:20:52,545
Someday, there might be problems.

259
00:20:52,625 --> 00:20:54,585
But the biggest shame is…

260
00:20:56,065 --> 00:20:57,705
losing the friendship.

261
00:21:13,745 --> 00:21:14,625
I…

262
00:21:18,505 --> 00:21:19,505
I think

263
00:21:20,265 --> 00:21:23,505
the Lovers card is trying
to tell me something.

264
00:21:26,465 --> 00:21:27,905
You suddenly came to see me.

265
00:21:27,985 --> 00:21:29,465
Did you miss me?

266
00:21:32,585 --> 00:21:33,545
Faye.

267
00:21:34,705 --> 00:21:36,145
What's wrong, Indy?

268
00:21:37,345 --> 00:21:39,345
I have something to tell you.

269
00:21:45,625 --> 00:21:47,625
I don't have romantic feelings for you.

270
00:21:50,425 --> 00:21:52,265
Did I do something wrong?

271
00:21:53,345 --> 00:21:54,545
Faye, you did nothing wrong.

272
00:21:55,065 --> 00:21:59,145
It's just, I was so excited
about dating you,

273
00:21:59,825 --> 00:22:02,705
but once we actually did,
I realized it wasn't love.

274
00:22:03,745 --> 00:22:05,745
So I don't want you to get hurt

275
00:22:05,825 --> 00:22:09,145
or waste your time… on me.

276
00:22:11,585 --> 00:22:13,505
Is it really that simple?

277
00:22:18,785 --> 00:22:20,105
I'm sorry.

278
00:22:20,625 --> 00:22:21,865
I was wrong.

279
00:22:32,945 --> 00:22:34,065
Let's break up.

280
00:22:36,345 --> 00:22:37,905
But just so you know,

281
00:22:37,985 --> 00:22:42,585
I'm the one breaking up with you,
not you dumping me.

282
00:22:56,265 --> 00:22:57,865
How dare you break up with my sister?

283
00:22:58,865 --> 00:23:00,425
You're exactly like your friend.

284
00:23:03,865 --> 00:23:06,945
Faye, you're better off
without someone like him.

285
00:23:10,585 --> 00:23:11,785
Goodbye.

286
00:23:11,865 --> 00:23:13,305
Stop chasing after my sister.

287
00:23:13,385 --> 00:23:17,545
FOOD - LETTER - PACKAGE

288
00:23:22,665 --> 00:23:23,745
Yes!

289
00:23:38,945 --> 00:23:42,265
Loving yourself never hurts.

290
00:23:42,345 --> 00:23:45,345
Some people are like waste in your body.

291
00:23:45,425 --> 00:23:47,345
You need to detox them all out.

292
00:23:47,865 --> 00:23:49,505
Let's take better care of ourselves.

293
00:23:51,545 --> 00:23:52,625
Whoa.

294
00:23:53,625 --> 00:23:54,745
-Damn.
-Shit.

295
00:23:54,825 --> 00:23:57,185
You became a meme overnight.

296
00:23:59,305 --> 00:24:00,265
Look.

297
00:24:02,465 --> 00:24:03,785
My life is over.

298
00:24:06,785 --> 00:24:08,225
It's not just you, dude.

299
00:24:08,945 --> 00:24:10,505
I'm getting dragged into this too.

300
00:24:11,025 --> 00:24:13,825
This group of guys is something else.

301
00:24:13,905 --> 00:24:15,905
Change the name from
"You'll Get Used to It"

302
00:24:15,985 --> 00:24:17,585
to "You'll Just Be Worthless."

303
00:24:24,145 --> 00:24:25,225
Come on.

304
00:24:26,025 --> 00:24:27,265
Your planet's in retrograde.

305
00:24:28,345 --> 00:24:31,705
It's a time when things swept
under the rug tend to come out.

306
00:24:35,305 --> 00:24:37,145
What's been swept under the rug?

307
00:24:38,305 --> 00:24:42,465
Like, unresolved feelings,

308
00:24:42,545 --> 00:24:45,385
the truth, things like that.

309
00:24:49,265 --> 00:24:50,305
Wait.

310
00:24:51,305 --> 00:24:53,105
Lee got back together with Putter,

311
00:24:54,385 --> 00:24:56,305
and Indy broke up with Faye.

312
00:24:56,825 --> 00:24:58,745
Shit.

313
00:24:59,465 --> 00:25:01,585
The universe is for real, fortune teller.

314
00:25:03,705 --> 00:25:05,025
I'll read your cards for you.

315
00:25:05,545 --> 00:25:06,785
I'll give you 50% off.

316
00:25:07,305 --> 00:25:09,265
Didn't you say you were
afraid I'd get hooked on tarot,

317
00:25:09,345 --> 00:25:10,465
so you wanted me to live my own life?

318
00:25:10,545 --> 00:25:12,225
I've diagnosed you,

319
00:25:12,745 --> 00:25:14,465
and your condition is too severe.

320
00:25:15,545 --> 00:25:16,625
Fine.

321
00:25:17,145 --> 00:25:19,025
Maybe I should get a reading from you.

322
00:25:28,105 --> 00:25:28,985
What?

323
00:25:29,585 --> 00:25:31,225
You guys, get out.

324
00:25:31,305 --> 00:25:32,945
Jia needs to concentrate.

325
00:25:35,345 --> 00:25:37,625
Did he forget this is my room?

326
00:25:45,265 --> 00:25:48,385
Pick three cards
and ask them what you want to know.

327
00:25:50,625 --> 00:25:54,465
Well, love, I guess.

328
00:26:06,425 --> 00:26:08,425
You're still naive about love.

329
00:26:09,465 --> 00:26:11,905
You might need to be braver
to move forward.

330
00:26:13,825 --> 00:26:17,625
Hey, the cards say you'll find pure love.

331
00:26:20,145 --> 00:26:22,025
New opportunities are coming your way.

332
00:26:24,265 --> 00:26:26,345
So, do the cards say

333
00:26:26,865 --> 00:26:28,825
if it's a close friend
or someone close to me?

334
00:26:33,305 --> 00:26:34,265
Why?

335
00:26:35,065 --> 00:26:36,745
Do you like someone close to you?

336
00:26:39,265 --> 00:26:40,385
I guess.

337
00:26:45,905 --> 00:26:47,145
How close?

338
00:26:54,065 --> 00:26:55,305
One foot.

339
00:27:05,345 --> 00:27:06,625
Ten centimeters.

340
00:27:12,385 --> 00:27:13,505
Five centimeters.

341
00:27:40,265 --> 00:27:41,225
Isn't that too close?

342
00:27:47,265 --> 00:27:48,425
Dude,

343
00:27:49,465 --> 00:27:52,625
they've got some serious chemistry.

344
00:27:53,825 --> 00:27:55,585
You're really into this, aren't you?

345
00:27:55,665 --> 00:27:59,585
I guess I've been around Min too much.

346
00:28:00,105 --> 00:28:01,265
I'm so into this.

347
00:28:01,345 --> 00:28:02,745
Hashtag "JiaIn."

348
00:28:02,825 --> 00:28:07,425
-Or should it be hashtag "InJia"?
-Stop shaking me!

349
00:28:07,945 --> 00:28:08,865
Fine.

350
00:28:19,585 --> 00:28:20,705
Hello, babe.

351
00:28:20,785 --> 00:28:21,785
Where is everyone else?

352
00:28:22,305 --> 00:28:24,345
Everyone else?
I don't want them seeing you.

353
00:28:25,025 --> 00:28:25,865
I'm possessive.

354
00:28:25,945 --> 00:28:27,425
Possessive of what?

355
00:28:27,505 --> 00:28:29,905
What? With a cute face like yours,

356
00:28:29,985 --> 00:28:31,545
how could I not be?

357
00:28:32,945 --> 00:28:34,025
Oh, right.

358
00:28:34,105 --> 00:28:35,545
When are you coming back?

359
00:28:35,625 --> 00:28:36,825
I'm dying here.

360
00:28:37,545 --> 00:28:39,345
Just count down till I come back.

361
00:28:39,425 --> 00:28:41,385
I don't know when I'll be back yet.

362
00:28:41,465 --> 00:28:45,145
Oh, have you talked to your parents yet
about school?

363
00:28:48,625 --> 00:28:49,985
Not yet.

364
00:28:50,065 --> 00:28:51,985
I haven't found the right time.

365
00:28:52,065 --> 00:28:53,505
I don't know when to bring it up.

366
00:28:54,345 --> 00:28:55,545
You know that

367
00:28:57,425 --> 00:28:58,945
I'm always on your side, right?

368
00:29:04,145 --> 00:29:05,425
Give me your address.

369
00:29:05,505 --> 00:29:06,865
I'll send you some food.

370
00:29:06,945 --> 00:29:08,185
Stop it.

371
00:29:08,265 --> 00:29:11,385
Since I came back here,
I've been eating so much healthy food.

372
00:29:11,465 --> 00:29:13,105
Hey, don't get too skinny.

373
00:29:13,625 --> 00:29:15,665
I won't have your puppy belly to pinch.

374
00:29:16,425 --> 00:29:18,265
You're so mean.

375
00:29:19,265 --> 00:29:20,705
-Hey.
-What?

376
00:29:20,785 --> 00:29:23,305
Are you not gonna let us
talk to Putter at all?

377
00:29:23,945 --> 00:29:25,065
Hi, Putter.

378
00:29:26,385 --> 00:29:28,985
Putter, I want some pork rinds.
Bring me some.

379
00:29:30,585 --> 00:29:32,585
Hey, I'm talking to my boyfriend.

380
00:29:32,665 --> 00:29:33,745
Go away.

381
00:29:35,065 --> 00:29:35,945
Go.

382
00:29:36,025 --> 00:29:39,305
Wow, you can call him your boyfriend
so easily now.

383
00:29:39,385 --> 00:29:40,785
Yeah.

384
00:29:40,865 --> 00:29:41,705
Something stinks.

385
00:29:42,385 --> 00:29:43,905
Must be the smell of love.

386
00:29:43,985 --> 00:29:45,305
These two too.

387
00:29:45,385 --> 00:29:47,625
Oh, yeah. What's going on with these two?

388
00:29:47,705 --> 00:29:50,785
-Hey, stop pinching me.
-Do it again.

389
00:30:14,065 --> 00:30:16,025
Wow, that smells so good.

390
00:30:17,865 --> 00:30:19,345
It's a grain salad, sweetheart.

391
00:30:19,425 --> 00:30:21,625
I saw them make it in a vertical drama.

392
00:30:21,705 --> 00:30:23,545
It looked good, so I tried making it.

393
00:30:23,625 --> 00:30:25,025
Just a minute, sweetheart.

394
00:30:32,145 --> 00:30:33,345
Why are you standing there?

395
00:30:33,985 --> 00:30:35,025
Is something wrong?

396
00:30:40,145 --> 00:30:41,985
Dad. Mom.

397
00:30:43,665 --> 00:30:45,625
I don't want to study
architecture anymore.

398
00:30:53,145 --> 00:30:56,145
I understand.
You don't have to rush, Putter.

399
00:30:56,225 --> 00:30:57,945
You still have two years.

400
00:30:59,105 --> 00:31:00,745
That's not what I mean, Mom.

401
00:31:00,825 --> 00:31:04,225
I mean, I've found something I want to do,

402
00:31:04,305 --> 00:31:06,185
but I don't know
if you'll be okay with it.

403
00:31:12,345 --> 00:31:13,545
Here.

404
00:31:16,545 --> 00:31:19,545
-Fire Storm!
-Oh, Do you compete in esports too?

405
00:31:19,625 --> 00:31:21,065
Yeah.

406
00:31:21,145 --> 00:31:22,585
That's a big match

407
00:31:22,665 --> 00:31:24,385
I just won.

408
00:31:26,905 --> 00:31:28,345
If it makes you happy,

409
00:31:28,865 --> 00:31:30,545
I'll support you all the way.

410
00:31:31,545 --> 00:31:32,545
Right, honey?

411
00:31:41,105 --> 00:31:42,145
Putter,

412
00:31:42,225 --> 00:31:44,105
if you don't want to study architecture,

413
00:31:44,185 --> 00:31:47,585
why not try business or engineering?

414
00:31:50,985 --> 00:31:52,385
Maybe, Mom.

415
00:31:52,985 --> 00:31:55,545
But, I have my own dream now.

416
00:31:56,785 --> 00:31:58,425
I want to be an esports player.

417
00:31:59,345 --> 00:32:01,025
I enjoy playing games.

418
00:32:03,185 --> 00:32:04,865
I'm not saying you can't, Putter.

419
00:32:05,385 --> 00:32:07,345
I see you playing games all the time.

420
00:32:09,145 --> 00:32:10,705
I'm just worried

421
00:32:11,745 --> 00:32:13,505
that if you choose this path,

422
00:32:13,585 --> 00:32:15,545
what will your future look like?

423
00:32:17,025 --> 00:32:18,145
I understand, Mom.

424
00:32:23,185 --> 00:32:25,665
Take it easy.
We can talk about this later.

425
00:32:31,265 --> 00:32:34,505
Mom's probably shocked
because you just dropped that on her.

426
00:32:36,305 --> 00:32:37,785
I didn't know how to tell them.

427
00:32:39,785 --> 00:32:41,065
What about those prep classes?

428
00:32:41,145 --> 00:32:42,305
Didn't you like them at all?

429
00:32:42,825 --> 00:32:44,425
It's not that I didn't like them.

430
00:32:45,345 --> 00:32:46,945
They were fun.

431
00:32:49,225 --> 00:32:51,265
But playing games excites me more.

432
00:32:57,505 --> 00:32:59,105
Pim, here.

433
00:33:01,385 --> 00:33:03,385
I guess that's your passion.

434
00:33:03,905 --> 00:33:06,505
It's good that you know what you like.

435
00:33:08,665 --> 00:33:09,705
Yeah.

436
00:33:11,665 --> 00:33:12,665
Done.

437
00:33:15,745 --> 00:33:18,265
Putter, play for me sometime.

438
00:33:18,345 --> 00:33:19,785
I like watching game streams too.

439
00:33:20,705 --> 00:33:22,185
You know about streamers too?

440
00:33:23,345 --> 00:33:25,065
I'm waiting to send you coins, Putter.

441
00:33:26,505 --> 00:33:27,785
Thanks.

442
00:33:29,065 --> 00:33:31,345
Don't worry too much.
Mom will come around.

443
00:33:32,385 --> 00:33:33,985
Pink, come play downstairs with me.

444
00:33:35,345 --> 00:33:36,305
Thanks, guys.

445
00:33:36,385 --> 00:33:38,185
-Let's go.
-Good luck, Putter.

446
00:33:38,265 --> 00:33:39,425
Thank you, little Sis.

447
00:33:54,265 --> 00:33:55,905
I talked to my parents.

448
00:33:55,985 --> 00:33:57,385
It didn't go too well.

449
00:34:00,785 --> 00:34:03,225
When you're free, give me a call.

450
00:34:05,505 --> 00:34:06,865
Where did he go?

451
00:34:39,185 --> 00:34:42,025
Hello? Where the hell have you been?

452
00:34:42,545 --> 00:34:46,945
Is your house
the one with the big black gate?

453
00:34:47,465 --> 00:34:49,225
Yeah. How did you know?

454
00:34:51,105 --> 00:34:52,625
Thank you.

455
00:34:53,385 --> 00:34:56,065
Wow, your whole family is good-looking.

456
00:34:56,665 --> 00:34:58,345
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

457
00:35:05,745 --> 00:35:09,545
Thank you so much
for always looking after Putter.

458
00:35:09,625 --> 00:35:10,585
Oh,

459
00:35:10,665 --> 00:35:12,505
we should be thanking Putter.

460
00:35:12,585 --> 00:35:16,025
He's the one who keeps LeeIth in line.

461
00:35:16,105 --> 00:35:17,505
Without Putter,

462
00:35:17,585 --> 00:35:19,985
Lee would never have
straightened himself out.

463
00:35:20,905 --> 00:35:22,505
You're ruining my image.

464
00:35:23,505 --> 00:35:24,385
But it's true, isn't it?

465
00:35:24,465 --> 00:35:26,825
Otherwise, would you
have gotten serious enough

466
00:35:26,905 --> 00:35:29,665
to become a trainee at a record label?

467
00:35:30,345 --> 00:35:32,305
Wait, they accepted you?

468
00:35:32,385 --> 00:35:33,705
Yeah.

469
00:35:35,225 --> 00:35:37,345
But honestly, it was Putter

470
00:35:37,425 --> 00:35:41,145
who made me realize
that following your dreams is possible.

471
00:35:43,185 --> 00:35:44,585
Honestly,

472
00:35:44,665 --> 00:35:49,305
at first, I was the one who wasn't sure

473
00:35:49,385 --> 00:35:52,785
if playing music
would give him a stable future.

474
00:35:53,585 --> 00:35:57,145
I sent him to Watthana Kunlaya School
because I wanted him to be a doctor.

475
00:35:58,105 --> 00:36:00,625
But when I saw him playing music and…

476
00:36:01,185 --> 00:36:02,985
how happy he was,

477
00:36:03,505 --> 00:36:04,785
I thought,

478
00:36:04,865 --> 00:36:07,225
how could I stop him?

479
00:36:09,505 --> 00:36:12,065
Oh, you compete in esports too?

480
00:36:12,745 --> 00:36:13,985
Yeah.

481
00:36:14,065 --> 00:36:15,505
That's a big match

482
00:36:15,585 --> 00:36:17,265
I just won.

483
00:36:18,425 --> 00:36:22,025
If it makes you happy,
I'll support you all the way.

484
00:36:22,985 --> 00:36:23,945
Right, honey?

485
00:36:30,665 --> 00:36:32,985
Then I guess it's like Putter
when he plays video games.

486
00:36:33,505 --> 00:36:35,305
He looks so happy.

487
00:36:39,225 --> 00:36:42,265
Putter, when you're close to graduating,

488
00:36:42,345 --> 00:36:44,265
if your dream is still the same,

489
00:36:46,465 --> 00:36:48,745
then I'll support you all the way.

490
00:36:50,425 --> 00:36:51,425
Really, Mom?

491
00:36:51,505 --> 00:36:52,625
Of course, sweetheart.

492
00:36:53,265 --> 00:36:56,145
But, there's one condition.

493
00:36:56,905 --> 00:36:59,745
You still have to prep for architecture,

494
00:37:00,425 --> 00:37:02,465
and keep practicing your
drawing skills just in case.

495
00:37:02,545 --> 00:37:05,705
Just think of it as a hobby.

496
00:37:06,825 --> 00:37:09,825
Of course. I'll be there
studying with him too.

497
00:37:11,145 --> 00:37:12,265
You'll only disturb him.

498
00:37:16,745 --> 00:37:18,665
You'll just distract Putter.

499
00:37:27,985 --> 00:37:29,825
We're bonding.

500
00:37:30,345 --> 00:37:32,465
We get along pretty well.

501
00:37:32,545 --> 00:37:34,465
-If I stay up too late, he complains.
-You ready?

502
00:37:34,985 --> 00:37:36,225
-I'm always ready.
-Let's go.

503
00:37:36,305 --> 00:37:37,985
-I have to turn off the big light first.
-Right?

504
00:37:39,865 --> 00:37:41,665
I can't stay up late. He always complains.

505
00:37:44,505 --> 00:37:45,585
He scolds me too.

506
00:37:45,665 --> 00:37:47,745
"Turn off the light. It hurts my eyes."

507
00:37:53,065 --> 00:37:54,665
Dad, Mom.

508
00:37:56,385 --> 00:37:57,345
I have something to tell you.

509
00:38:04,145 --> 00:38:06,665
When I first moved to Bangkok,

510
00:38:07,785 --> 00:38:10,665
I… acted like I could handle it,

511
00:38:11,185 --> 00:38:13,785
but honestly, I was scared.

512
00:38:14,865 --> 00:38:16,025
Scared I wouldn't fit in with my friends.

513
00:38:17,745 --> 00:38:19,385
Scared I'd feel like an outsider.

514
00:38:28,105 --> 00:38:29,785
But when I met Lee,

515
00:38:30,825 --> 00:38:32,585
he made all my worries disappear.

516
00:38:34,465 --> 00:38:36,065
Lee is someone important to me.

517
00:38:38,985 --> 00:38:40,865
And I want to tell you that

518
00:38:42,225 --> 00:38:43,425
Lee…

519
00:38:44,585 --> 00:38:46,305
isn't just my best friend.

520
00:38:50,545 --> 00:38:51,905
He's my boyfriend.

521
00:39:45,265 --> 00:39:48,825
Then please treat Putter like
another son of yours.

522
00:39:49,945 --> 00:39:51,705
I'd be more than happy to.

523
00:39:51,785 --> 00:39:52,985
But actually,

524
00:39:53,065 --> 00:39:55,785
I'm the one who should be leaving
Lee in Putter's hands.

525
00:39:57,185 --> 00:39:58,345
Lee,

526
00:39:58,425 --> 00:40:00,825
make sure you keep Putter in line.

527
00:40:01,865 --> 00:40:04,985
Don't let Putter neglect his studies
until he's a full-time esports player.

528
00:40:05,625 --> 00:40:06,585
Okay?

529
00:40:07,985 --> 00:40:09,545
What kind of person
do you think your son is?

530
00:40:16,665 --> 00:40:17,825
Everyone,

531
00:40:17,905 --> 00:40:20,985
let's celebrate, then.

532
00:40:23,825 --> 00:40:25,665
-Come on.
-Let's go, Mom!

533
00:40:25,745 --> 00:40:26,585
Here comes my child!

534
00:40:26,665 --> 00:40:28,265
Come on.

535
00:40:28,345 --> 00:40:29,425
Thank you.

536
00:41:11,545 --> 00:41:12,545
Hey.

537
00:41:12,625 --> 00:41:14,385
I've been thinking.

538
00:41:15,625 --> 00:41:17,465
If you're serious
about being an esports player,

539
00:41:17,985 --> 00:41:19,425
you'll need a room to practice.

540
00:41:20,545 --> 00:41:21,785
